{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-preact"},{"type":"text","value":". Import the UI factory from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-preact/ui"},{"type":"text","value":". Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createChatHook({ options, ...components })"},{"type":"text","value":" once at module scope. Your app calls "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useAppChat()"},{"type":"text","value":" to create the instance. Render "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<chat.AppChat />"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The factory API matches "},{"type":"link","href":"./react","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Widgets are Preact components. Import hooks from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"preact/hooks"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"preact/compat"},{"type":"text","value":" in your widgets if you need them."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The factory needs a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolsComponents"},{"type":"text","value":" entry for every tool name in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chatOptions"},{"type":"text","value":". It also needs an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interruptsComponents.generic"},{"type":"text","value":" entry for every interrupt id. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generic.fallback"},{"type":"text","value":" is optional."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The server route matches the "},{"type":"link","href":"./react","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React page"}]},{"type":"text","value":". The "},{"type":"link","href":"./recipes/index","children":[{"type":"text","value":"chat UI recipes"}]},{"type":"text","value":" show the same option groups. The code there is React, and the shape carries over."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"client","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-preact'\nimport { createChatHook } from '@tanstack/ai-preact/ui'\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst getWeather = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'getWeather',\n  description: 'Look up weather',\n  inputSchema: z.object({ city: z.string() }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({ temperature: z.number() }),\n}).client()\n\nconst chatOptions = {\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n  tools: [getWeather],\n}\n\nconst { useAppChat } = createChatHook({\n  options: chatOptions,\n  components: {\n    layout: (props) => (\n      <main>\n        <props.Messages />\n        <props.Interrupts />\n        <props.Queue />\n      </main>\n    ),\n    message: (props) => (\n      <article>\n        <props.Parts />\n      </article>\n    ),\n  },\n  partsComponents: { fallback: (props) => <span>{props.part.type}</span> },\n  toolsComponents: {\n    getWeather: (props) => <strong>{props.part.input?.city}</strong>,\n  },\n})\n\nexport function ChatScreen() {\n  const chat = useAppChat()\n  return <chat.AppChat />\n}","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"client","text":"Client","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nInstall `@tanstack/ai-preact`. Import the UI factory from `@tanstack/ai-preact/ui`. Call `createChatHook({ options, ...components })` once at module scope. Your app calls `useAppChat()` to create the instance. Render `<chat.AppChat />`.\n\nThe factory API matches [React](./react). Widgets are Preact components. Import hooks from `preact/hooks` or `preact/compat` in your widgets if you need them.\n\nThe factory needs a `toolsComponents` entry for every tool name in `chatOptions`. It also needs an `interruptsComponents.generic` entry for every interrupt id. `generic.fallback` is optional.\n\nThe server route matches the [React page](./react). The [chat UI recipes](./recipes/index) show the same option groups. The code there is React, and the shape carries over.\n\n## Client\n\n```tsx\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-preact'\nimport { createChatHook } from '@tanstack/ai-preact/ui'\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst getWeather = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'getWeather',\n  description: 'Look up weather',\n  inputSchema: z.object({ city: z.string() }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({ temperature: z.number() }),\n}).client()\n\nconst chatOptions = {\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n  tools: [getWeather],\n}\n\nconst { useAppChat } = createChatHook({\n  options: chatOptions,\n  components: {\n    layout: (props) => (\n      <main>\n        <props.Messages />\n        <props.Interrupts />\n        <props.Queue />\n      </main>\n    ),\n    message: (props) => (\n      <article>\n        <props.Parts />\n      </article>\n    ),\n  },\n  partsComponents: { fallback: (props) => <span>{props.part.type}</span> },\n  toolsComponents: {\n    getWeather: (props) => <strong>{props.part.input?.city}</strong>,\n  },\n})\n\nexport function ChatScreen() {\n  const chat = useAppChat()\n  return <chat.AppChat />\n}\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Preact Chat UI\nid: typed-headless-ui-preact\norder: 5\ndescription: \"Build a typed, headless Preact chat UI with createChatHook. The API matches React.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - createChatHook\n  - preact\n  - headless ui\n  - ToolProps\n---\n\nInstall `@tanstack/ai-preact`. Import the UI factory from `@tanstack/ai-preact/ui`. Call `createChatHook({ options, ...components })` once at module scope. Your app calls `useAppChat()` to create the instance. Render `<chat.AppChat />`.\n\nThe factory API matches [React](./react). Widgets are Preact components. Import hooks from `preact/hooks` or `preact/compat` in your widgets if you need them.\n\nThe factory needs a `toolsComponents` entry for every tool name in `chatOptions`. It also needs an `interruptsComponents.generic` entry for every interrupt id. `generic.fallback` is optional.\n\nThe server route matches the [React page](./react). The [chat UI recipes](./recipes/index) show the same option groups. The code there is React, and the shape carries over.\n\n## Client\n\n```tsx\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-preact'\nimport { createChatHook } from '@tanstack/ai-preact/ui'\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst getWeather = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'getWeather',\n  description: 'Look up weather',\n  inputSchema: z.object({ city: z.string() }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({ temperature: z.number() }),\n}).client()\n\nconst chatOptions = {\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n  tools: [getWeather],\n}\n\nconst { useAppChat } = createChatHook({\n  options: chatOptions,\n  components: {\n    layout: (props) => (\n      <main>\n        <props.Messages />\n        <props.Interrupts />\n        <props.Queue />\n      </main>\n    ),\n    message: (props) => (\n      <article>\n        <props.Parts />\n      </article>\n    ),\n  },\n  partsComponents: { fallback: (props) => <span>{props.part.type}</span> },\n  toolsComponents: {\n    getWeather: (props) => <strong>{props.part.input?.city}</strong>,\n  },\n})\n\nexport function ChatScreen() {\n  const chat = useAppChat()\n  return <chat.AppChat />\n}\n```\n"}
